    "description": "Vintage Promotional Wall Calendar Lot\nThe Travelers & Northwestern Mutual Life Insurance\nPaper & Cardboard Ephemera, Circa 1950s\nThis estate collection features vintage 1950s promotional wall calendars and art prints issued by prominent American insurance firms, including The Travelers Insurance Company of Hartford, Connecticut, and The Northwestern Mutual Life Insurance Company. Highly regarded for their high-quality lithographic reproductions, these corporate calendars showcased classic American artwork, including Currier & Ives historical lithographs and John James Audubon wildlife plates.\nItems Included:\n1953 The Travelers wall calendar featuring Currier & Ives prints such as \"The Home of Washington, Mount Vernon, Va.\" and \"Morning in the Woods\"\n1957 The Northwestern Mutual Life Insurance Company Centennial Anniversary calendar with Audubon \"Mallard Duck\" artwork\nStandalone illustrated botanical art sheet featuring a detailed green oak tree\nMultiple rolled calendar tubes and original postal shipping tubes housed in a cardboard storage box\nCondition:\nPaper shows vintage toning, edge curling, foxing, and age-related wear consistent with rolled storage. Outer paper sleeves and mailing tubes display tears, fraying, tape residue, and chipping. Prints retain clear details and legible typography. Hanging metal strips and eyelets present on calendars.",
